        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "39f39d48-e6a4-5ab4-b64c-8599271fbf1d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Seán Heuston, Con Colbert\n- Organizations: Fianna Éireann\n- Places: Kilmainham Gaol, Dublin\n- Events: Easter Rising of 1916\n\nFacts:\n- Seán Heuston, born Jack Heuston and also known as J. J. Heuston, was born on 21 February 1891 and was an Irish rebel and a member of Fianna Éireann.\n- Seán Heuston took part in the Easter Rising of 1916.\n- Many Irish revolutionaries, including leaders of the 1916 Easter Rising, were imprisoned and executed by the British in Kilmainham Gaol.\n- Seán Heuston was executed by firing squad in Kilmainham Gaol on 8 May 1916.\n- Con Colbert was shot by firing squad in Kilmainham Gaol, Dublin, on 8 May 1916 for his part in the 1916 Easter Rising.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "5fbf4c8f-c17e-5fcd-83de-f9bbb3aae4e4",
